The Man

The Man has never shook it out under a log or boat. The Man has never cheated an evolution or himself. The Man doesn’t care how cold or choppy his Mother Ocean is. He just makes the times better and better each swim.

The Man feels the pain of the soft sand and the hard rocks, but he overcomes them both with certainty and confidence. The Man feels the fear of the failing breath in his lungs under nine feet of water as he is constantly assaulted but his composure is steadfast and his confidence unparalleled as he carries out his objective.

The Man does not get motivated. He is motivated, and until we can be more like The Man, we will pay him.

The Man does not accept cash, check, or credit card. The Man only accepts blood, sweat and tears. Frog Men have been paying The Man for generations for their mistakes, all of which are avoidable. We thank The Man for collecting blood, sweat, and tears now, so we do not have to pay with our life later.